<title>UK: UK air freight rises four percent in 1996.</title>
<headline>UK air freight rises four percent in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freight traffic at all British airports rose four percent to 1.783 million tonnes last year against from 1.717 million tonnes in 1995, annual Civil Aviation Authority's (CAA) data shows.</p>
<p>The vast bulk of freight at British airpoirts goes through London airports with Heathrow alone accounting for 1.04 million tonnes last year. Ten years ago total freight at UK airports was 730,000 tomnnes with Heathrow accounting for 537,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>Details in thousands of tonnes excluding transit cargo for 1996, 1995 and 1986 include:</p>
<p>London	    1996	1995    Pct change   1986</p>
<p>Airports				  '96 vs '95</p>
<p>Gatwick	    267	 230     up    16    164</p>
<p>Heathrow	 1,040     1,032		-    537</p>
<p>Luton		 19	  14     up    33	6</p>
<p>Stansted	   105	  90     up    16     13</p>
<p>Total London   1,434     1,370     up     5    730</p>
<p>Other airports</p>
<p>Belfast Inter     27	  31     down  12     23</p>
<p>Birmingham	  19	  21     down   8	7</p>
<p>Coventry	    23	  32     down  30    nil</p>
<p>East Midlands    105	  83     up    27     20</p>
<p>Glasgow	     12	  13     down  11     13</p>
<p>Liverpool	   28	  32     down  10	7</p>
<p>Manchester	  79	  80     down   2     39</p>
<p>Prestwick	   22	  20     up     9     10</p>
<p>Total other	349	 347	-	    151</p>
<p>airports</p>
<p>Total UK	 1,783	1,717    up    4	881</p>
<p>airports</p>
